%[text] ## ![](text:image:4dbe) **Application 2. Bioreactor**
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Bioreactor cartoon](text:image:62bf)
%[text] Bioreactors are commonly operated at fixed conditions of pH, aeration, and substrate concentration. At a fixed set of these conditions, the **product titer after 24 hours** depends primarily on the **bioreactor temperature**. Over the normal operating range, this relationship can be approximated by a **quadratic polynomial**:
%[text] $P=aT^2+bT+c${"altText":"P=aT^2+bT+c"}
%[text] where
%[text] - $P${"altText":"P"} is the product titer after 24 h (g/L)
%[text] - $T${"altText":"T"} is the reactor temperature (°C)
%[text] - $a,b,\\text{and }c${"altText":"a,b,\text{and }c"} are empirical model parameters \
%[text] ### Load Bioreactor Data
